{
  "meta": {
    "id": "t2_03",
    "tier": 2,
    "order_in_tier": 3,
    "title": "Melancholy Broken Chords",
    "composer_source": "Cornelius Gurlitt / Czerny Minor Study",
    "key": {
      "fifths": 1,
      "mode": "minor"
    },
    "time_signature": {
      "numerator": 4,
      "denominator": 4
    },
    "target_bpm": 80.0,
    "theory": {
      "summary": "Flowing E-minor broken-chord study drilling the natural minor i-VI-III-VII progression and B7 cadence.",
      "pattern_tip": "Hear the descending bass roots E -> C -> G -> D in Phrase A, then watch for D# on the V7 (B7) cadence.",
      "technique_tip": "Shape each 8th-note arpeggio with a single supple wrist circle rather than poking individual fingers.",
      "ballade_link": "Builds left-hand arpeggio fluency and natural-minor harmonic recognition.",
      "concept_title": "Flowing Arpeggios & The Natural-Minor i - VI - III - VII Cycle",
      "concept_paragraphs": [
        "In Phrase A, notice a progression loved by both Romantic and modern film composers: Em -> C -> G -> D (i -> VI -> III -> VII). Instead of using a sharp leading tone yet, natural minor tumbles warmly downward along a resonant chain of relative chords.",
        "Only in Phrase B and C does D# enter inside B7 (V7), tightening the harmonic spring cleanly back into home E minor."
      ],
      "form_map": [
        {
          "phrase_label": "Phrase A (Bars 1-4)",
          "role": "Broken-chord E-minor cascade through the Aeolian cycle Em - C - G - D."
        },
        {
          "phrase_label": "Phrase B (Bars 5-8)",
          "role": "Shifts through G/B (III6) and Am (iv) to build to a dramatic D# B7 Dominant."
        },
        {
          "phrase_label": "Phrase C (Bars 9-12)",
          "role": "Combines natural minor v (Bm) with the full harmonic B7 -> Em resolution."
        }
      ],
      "practice_steps": [
        "1. Play through Skeleton mode to feel the root cascade (E -> C -> G -> D -> B).",
        "2. Shape LH 8th-note arpeggios with one slow circular wrist motion per bar.",
        "3. Spot D# in Bars 8 and 11 before playing so the harmonic minor turn shines.",
        "4. Perform smoothly at 80 BPM without chopping individual arpeggio notes."
      ],
      "audio_examples": [
        {
          "label": "Aeolian Cascade (i -> VI -> III -> VII)",
          "caption": "Em -> C -> G -> D",
          "chords": [
            "Em",
            "C",
            "G",
            "D"
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "Natural v vs. Harmonic Dominant V7",
          "caption": "Em -> Bm -> Em vs. Em -> B7 -> Em",
          "chords": [
            "Em",
            "Bm",
            "B7",
            "Em"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  },
